# im an obsessive learner — for domain terms 🦉📜

zoom-in of `im_an.obsessive_learner`: *what this domain calls a concept*. a term is a **word** (noun/verb/adj) that composes this repo's declared dobjs/dops; one entry per word, reused (`stone` serves `Stone`, `getStone`; `gen` serves every `gen*`). home: `.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/domain.terms/`.

whenever a term is discovered or debated (dobj/dop named, synonym argued, canonical word settled), crystallize it into the glossary. no gate carries this itch: run `rhx learn.domain.terms`.

## the moves

1. recall dobjs/dops you declared or engaged
2. split names into terms (`getStone` → verb `get` + noun `stone`)
3. itemize each NEW word as a `choice._.` cluster; for extant terms, extend `.refs`
4. record any synonym you judged; log a resolved dispute in `.reason`
5. articulate `progress.md`: what you distilled and why, or why none

## a settled term is NOT deferrable

| the round… | then |
|---|---|
| declared a repo-born dobj/dop | its terms get clusters this round |
| settled a synonym (A canonical, B forbidden) | the judgment lands in the term file this round |

defer only a word that wants deeper discovery or a dispute still open. never a settled term.

see: `template.domain-term` · `howto.domain-term-disputes` · `.for.domain.invariants` · `.for.domain.glyphs`
